            <ArticleTitle>Benchmark-Quality Atomization Energies for BeH and BeH2.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>649-653</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.jctc.6b01154</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The total atomization energies for BeH and BeH2 have been calculated using the Feller-Peterson-Dixon approach to better than ±1 kcal/mol. The calculations are based on CCSD(T) all-electron calculations extrapolated to the complete limit, and CCSDT and CCSDTQ corrections are included. A scalar relativistic correction and a diagonal Born-Oppenheimer correction are included. Accurate zero-point energies are used. The total atomization energies at 0 K are 47.7 kcal/mol for BeH and 140.0 kcal/mol for BeH2 with error of at most ±0.3 kcal/mol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
